Subject: [PATCH] ipa: initialize stage gain for exposure fallback

Initialize stageGain to the value already used when there are no gain stages.
This makes the fallback path explicit and avoids GCC's maybe-uninitialized
warning, which is fatal because libcamera builds with -Werror.

Upstream-Status: Pending

---
 src/ipa/libipa/exposure_mode_helper.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/ipa/libipa/exposure_mode_helper.cpp b/src/ipa/libipa/exposure_mode_helper.cpp
--- a/src/ipa/libipa/exposure_mode_helper.cpp
+++ b/src/ipa/libipa/exposure_mode_helper.cpp
@@ -166,7 +166,7 @@ ExposureModeHelper::splitExposure(utils::Duration exposure) const
 		return { minShutter_, minGain_, exposure / (minShutter_ * minGain_) };
 
 	utils::Duration shutter;
-	double stageGain;
+	double stageGain = 1.0;
 	double gain;
 
 	for (unsigned int stage = 0; stage < gains_.size(); stage++) {
-- 
